    {
      "id": "rcy5ak2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. BASIC CONCEPT"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Percentages serve as the foundational base for data interpretation, profit and loss, and interest calculations.",
        "Conversion rules allow quick transition between fractions, decimals, and percentage values.",
        "Percentage increase and decrease express relative change against an original base value.",
        "Successive percentage changes account for multiple sequential percentage variations on a quantity.",
        "Reverse percentage techniques are used to calculate original values prior to any given percentage change."
      ],
      "id": "of6mwbu"
    },
    {
      "id": "hdoh5be",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Percentage means 'per hundred'.<br></br>1% = 1/100",
        "Percentage is used to express increase or decrease, comparison, profit and loss, marks, population, growth, etc.<br></br><br></br><em>In SSC examination, percentage questions are direct, formula-based, and often linked with Ratio, Profit–Loss and Simple Interest.</em>"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "y5uydp1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. CONVERSION RULES"
    },
    {
      "id": "fife1sr",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Fraction to Percentage:<br></br>(a/b) × 100<br></br>Example: 3/5 = 60%",
        "Percentage to Fraction:<br></br>x% = x/100<br></br>Example: 25% = 1/4",
        "Decimal to Percentage:<br></br>Multiply the decimal by 100<br></br>Example: 0.75 = 75%"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "f51jhwu",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. IMPORTANT PERCENTAGE VALUES"
